---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CallToAction from '../../components/CallToAction.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import observatoryPhoto from '../../assets/communities/goddard/goddard-lake-afton-observatory-redit.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Goddard, Kansas Community Guide | Charity Menefee"
  description="A practical introduction to Goddard, Kansas, including its location west of Wichita, older Main Street core, residential growth, and property considerations."
  pageClass="page-interior page-goddard"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Community guide · Goddard"
    title="Small-town roots, with growth all around."
    intro="Goddard is its own city immediately west of Wichita, where an older community centered around Main Street meets substantial newer residential growth."
    image={observatoryPhoto}
    imageAlt="Lake Afton Observatory beneath the Milky Way near Goddard"
    variant="community"
    imagePosition="center 34%"
    imagePositionMobile="58% center"
  />

  <section class="section-space" aria-labelledby="goddard-overview-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Getting oriented</p>
        <h2 id="goddard-overview-title">An independent city on the west side of the metro.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Goddard is an incorporated city in western Sedgwick County, immediately west of the Wichita metro. US-54/400, commonly called Kellogg, is the primary east and west corridor connecting Goddard with Wichita.</p>
        <p>The city's physical setting includes an older, established community around Main Street and newer growth spreading beyond it. That contrast helps explain why properties in Goddard can differ considerably in age, development pattern, and surrounding infrastructure.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space section-surface" aria-labelledby="goddard-housing-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Housing in a growing city</p>
        <h2 id="goddard-housing-title">New residential development is changing the city's footprint.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Goddard includes older established housing as well as newer residential development. City records identify Arbor Creek South and Rustic Creek among the additions contributing to that changing footprint.</p>
        <p>Those names illustrate where growth has occurred, but they don't confirm current construction or availability. The age and type of development can affect the lot, surrounding infrastructure, included improvements, and any HOA or special-assessment obligations tied to a property.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space section-sage" aria-labelledby="goddard-character-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Local character and change</p>
        <h2 id="goddard-character-title">Main Street and the US-54 corridor tell different parts of the story.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Goddard was incorporated in 1910, and Main Street historically served as the city's primary business area. That older physical core remains an important point of contrast with the newer development expanding the community's footprint.</p>
        <p>Goddard Linear Park sits near Main Street, and the Prairie Sunset Trail passes through the park on its route east toward Wichita and west toward Garden Plain. The trail accommodates walking, running, and bicycling, adding a physical connection through the older part of the city.</p>
        <p>Along the US-54 corridor, the Genesis Sports Complex represents a newer side of Goddard's growth. Its tournament and recreation facilities extend that story beyond housing without replacing the city's older center.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space" aria-labelledby="goddard-practical-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Practical things to consider</p>
        <h2 id="goddard-practical-title">The development around a home can matter as much as its age.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Start by confirming whether a property is inside Goddard city limits and how it connects to US-54/400 and the roads you expect to use. Then compare the home's age, lot characteristics, utilities, maintenance needs, and development setting.</p>
        <p>For newer construction, verify what's included with the home and lot, which restrictions apply, and whether assessments, utility arrangements, or HOA obligations are connected to that address.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space section-surface" aria-labelledby="goddard-search-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading split-heading">
        <div data-reveal="left">
          <p class="eyebrow">Useful questions</p>
          <h2 id="goddard-search-title">What should you verify when looking in Goddard?</h2>
        </div>
        <p data-reveal="right">The answers can vary between an established property and a home in a newer or still-developing area.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="question-grid reveal-stagger">
        <li data-reveal="up">Is this property in an established part of Goddard or a newer development?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">For new construction, what's included with the home and lot, and are HOA requirements or special assessments tied to the property?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">How does the location connect to US-54/400 and the roads you'd actually use?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">Which details about the home's age, lot, utilities, maintenance, or restrictions need verification?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">If the surrounding area is still developing, which improvements or future phases should be reviewed?</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="shell next-community" aria-label="Community pages">
    <span>Keep exploring</span>
    <a href="/communities/">All communities <i aria-hidden="true">→</i></a>
  </nav>
  <CallToAction
    title="Have questions about a property in Goddard?"
    copy="If you're comparing communities or have questions about a specific property, tell me what you're considering. I’ll help you sort through the location and property details that matter."
  />
</BaseLayout>
